  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.8.5 -- Table column filtering gains more filter kinds, row-placed editors, and a server-side mode; data-tooltip restyled to match LabelTooltip. Additive for typical usage, with two narrow compatibility notes below for consumers using TableColumnFilter/PropertyColumn directly.\n\nNEW\n- Table filtering: Column.FilterText/TextFilterMatch (search box), Column.FilterDropdown (your own panel via TableFilterContext), FilterIcon, OnFilterDropdownOpenChange, FilterOnClose.\n- PropertyColumn.Filterable/FilterValuesFromData: derive a filter from the property type, or from DataSource's distinct values, instead of declaring one by hand.\n- Table.FilterPlacement = TableFilterPlacement.Row: always-visible per-column editors in a second header row, instead of funnel dropdowns.\n- Table.OnFiltersChanged/ClearFiltersAsync(): the every-column counterpart to OnFilterChanged. Dropdown extras: FilterSearch, FilterCheckAll, DefaultFilterValues/FilterResetToDefault.\n- Table.ClientSideFiltering = false: keeps the filter UI/events, stops the built-in row narrowing, for server-side filtering.\n- Every filter label/format (FilterRowLabelFormat, FilterResultAnnouncementFormat, FilterClearLabel, FilterMinLabel/FilterMaxLabel, FilterBoolAnyText/FilterBoolTrueText/FilterBoolFalseText, FilterSelectPlaceholder, FilterSearchPlaceholder, FilterEmptyText, FilterCheckAllLabel, FilterSelectedCountFormat, FilterContainsFormat/FilterStartsWithFormat/FilterEqualsFormat, FilterDateStartLabel/FilterDateEndLabel) is a Table parameter. FilterResultAnnouncementFormat is new: a role=\"status\" region announces it after every filter change, so an existing FilterOptions/OnFilter column gains an announcement it didn't have before -- set it to \"\" to silence (a null value throws).\n\nCHANGED\n- data-tooltip now matches LabelTooltip's dark chip (#262626/white, 6px radius) instead of a lighter bordered card.\n- TableColumnFilter<TItem> lost its own FilterButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedButtonLabelFormat/FilterAppliedLabel/FilterLabel parameters -- the accessible name now comes from Table's parameters of the same names. Only affects code that instantiates TableColumnFilter directly.\n- PropertyColumn<TItem,TProp> now annotates TProp with [DynamicallyAccessedMembers(DynamicallyAccessedMemberTypes.All)]. Concrete TProp=\"...\" markup is unaffected; a consumer generic forwarding its own unannotated TProp into PropertyColumn needs the same annotation to avoid IL2091 under trim analysis.\n\nFIXED (all pre-existing, from the 10.6.7/10.7.0 column filtering -- not regressions in this release)\n- Under ScrollY, the fixed-positioned filter dropdown stretched to the viewport's right edge -- the stylesheet's right: 0 anchor was never cleared.\n- The filter dropdown was clipped by .wss-table-wrapper on a table short enough with no ScrollY; it escapes on every open now, not only under ScrollY.\n- A runtime Column.FilterMultiple true -> false flip left the earlier multi-key selection applied (two checked radios in one group); it trims to the first key.\n- The header funnel button had no min-height floor, so a consumer `button { max-height: fit-content }` reset collapsed its fixed 24px height to the icon.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog",
